title: "ComPy: ocean-bottom seismic and pressure data toolbox"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aminian
    given-names: Mohammad-Amin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9192-2734"
version: 1.3.2.1
date-released: 2026-11-25
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohammadAmin-Aminian/ComPy"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.13380107"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24537180"
    description: "Zenodo archive of version 1.3.2.1. The DOI above (10.5281/zenodo.13380107) always resolves to the latest version."
abstract: "ComPy is an open Python toolbox for ocean-bottom seismic and pressure data. It turns broadband seismometer and pressure-gauge records into calibrated quantities and models: data cleaning, tilt and coherent-noise removal, pressure-gauge quality control and calibration, seafloor compliance, Bayesian shear-velocity inversion and a global atlas of seafloor pressure noise."
keywords:
  - seafloor compliance
  - ocean-bottom seismometer
  - differential pressure gauge
  - shear velocity
  - Bayesian inversion
  - seafloor pressure noise
license: GPL-3.0-only
